  "info": {
    "title": "Dishi API",
    "description": "The Dishi backend. Conventions:\n\n- Money is **integer KES**; no decimals anywhere.\n- Time is **UTC in the database**, `Africa/Nairobi` at the edge.\n- Phones are **E.164** (`+2547XXXXXXXX`).\n- Lists return `{ data, page: { nextCursor, hasMore } }` (cursor) or `{ data, page: { limit, offset, total } }` for admin tables.\n- Errors are RFC 7807 `application/problem+json` with a stable `code`: VALIDATION_FAILED, UNAUTHENTICATED, PERMISSION_DENIED, MFA_REQUIRED, STEP_UP_REQUIRED, ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED, NOT_FOUND, ORDER_STATE_CONFLICT, ITEM_SOLD_OUT, STORE_NOT_ACCEPTING, SLOT_FULL, COUPON_INVALID, PAYMENT_AMOUNT_MISMATCH, IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT, LAST_SUPERADMIN, PERMISSION_ESCALATION, RATE_LIMITED.\n- `X-Request-Id` is accepted and echoed; every error carries it.\n- `Idempotency-Key` is required on money-moving POSTs (from N5).\n- `X-Dishi-Context` (`customer`, `vendor:<uuid>`, `platform`) selects the active actor context and is re-validated on every request (from N2).\n\nIdentity is verified through Supabase Auth; call `POST /auth/sync` to synchronize the local profile.",
    "version": "0.1.0",
